-- title:
--   Smooth Igusa base model off the supersingular locus, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with `hq3 : q = 3`, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and have $w$-value of `jGeomGen κ M'` in `ssJSet q κ`. The hypothesis `hle` places the base-changed full level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` inside `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`. Next, `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue map onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with the scaling and divisor-transport clauses of that structure), and `hR₀` demands that this reduction be coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (residue A) y`. Further, $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ (`OIg`), $O^{\mathrm{ss}}$ (`OSS`) are families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed respectively by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$ and by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa family is pinned by four hypotheses: `hIg_inf` identifies $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line `lineInfty q` as a Gauss ring, $f$ belonging to it exactly when $f \cdot y = x$ for some Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero coefficientwise reduction; `hIg` says that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma$-translate of `lineInfty q` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says the family is injective; `hIg_perm` says that pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`, for any $\zeta'$ and any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, permutes the family. The supersingular (Drinfeld) family is pinned by `hSS_A` (a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ precisely when $x \in A$), by `hSS_over` (for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is nonnegative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb` has nonnegative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue is the value of $s$ at that `R₀`-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$), by `hSS_fix` (each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) and by `hSS_tr` (each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ for every $a \in A$). Moreover `R` is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` with `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` says that `R₀.integers` is the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ under the inclusion given by `hle`.
--
--   The arithmetic of the base is encoded as follows: $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a field of small constants $k_0$ between $\mathbb Q$ and $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`); a prime $\ell \geq 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally one single finite layer of constants is given: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $x \in A_1$ iff $x \in A$, $A_1$ being a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion, `fieldBar q M'` being regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, asserts the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$, a finite set $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$, and, for every place $Q$ of that field, a subring $S_Q$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A_1[X] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$ and a set $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   First, the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, and $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Second, $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and $W$ have the same cardinality. Third, there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` such that every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` has its image in `fieldBar q M'` inside `R.integers` with $R$-residue $j(R_0\text{-residue of } f)$, and such that $Q \in N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ precisely when there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$. Fourth, every valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` which contains all the constants from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and is not the whole field is a principal ideal ring. Fifth, a linear disjointness statement: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   Sixth, for every place $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$: the map $A_1 \to \kappa$ sending $a$ to the residue of $a$ in $A$ is surjective; the image of every $a \in A_1$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is that image; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; $S_Q$ carries a local ring structure for which the kernel of $\chi_Q$ is the maximal ideal; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$, and conversely every element $f$ of that compositum satisfies $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_Q$ with $h \neq 0$; every element of $S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, and for every uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A_1$ an element $f$ of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` if and only if $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi)$ divides $f$ in $S_Q$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order equal to $1$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   Seventh, the discs are pairwise disjoint: for $Q, Q' \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, a place $P$ lying in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ forces $Q = Q'$. Eighth, equivariance under the level automorphisms: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced action `R.resAut τ` on places preserves membership in $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ in both directions, and for $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ one has `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (D Q)` $= D_{\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q}$. Ninth, invariance under inertia: for $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` preserving $K_1$ and for $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, the arithmetic Galois action of $\tau$ on `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` preserves $S_Q$ in both directions and leaves $\chi_Q$ unchanged. Tenth, branches are separated: if $g$ in the same subgroup generated by the level automorphisms does not fix $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ under pullback, then for $Q, Q' \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and $P \in D_Q$ one has $g \cdot P \notin D_{Q'}$.
--
--   Eleventh, the discs avoid the supersingular tubes: for $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, $P \in D_Q$ and $s \in W$, it is not the case that both of the following hold, where the first concerns the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`, and the second the corresponding element for `qExpand ℚ M' jq`: the element lies in the valuation subring of $P$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen κ M'` (respectively at `jNGeomGen κ M'`), the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that element and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Twelfth, a covering statement: if a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ fails, for every $s \in W$, the condition that for all $f \in$ `R₀.integers` with nonnegative order wherever the `coeffEmb` image of `jq` has nonnegative order and with `R₀`-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and all $a \in A$ whose residue is the value of $s$ at that residue, the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ — then there are $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $\cdot\, P \in D_Q$. Thirteenth, there is a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar`, the subring of elements of nonnegative $q$-expansion order, together with a place $Q \notin N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with $P \in D_Q$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance of the base-model step on the Igusa branch of the semistable covering of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$: over one finite layer $K_1$ of constants it produces the stalks $S_Q$ at the smooth points of the Igusa component, with étale coordinate $\varphi_Q$, residue character $\chi_Q$ and the associated residue discs $D_Q$, all compatible with the level automorphisms and with inertia. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaTower_smoothPointData_of_stable_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaTower_smoothPointData_of_stable_of_eq_three), which assembles these data over the tower of constant layers.
